#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6e692dca-1bbc-59e7-999f-4acb806ddd38" :question/math-academy-id "e-8369" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =7\\arcsch(1-x),$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsch x) = -\\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|1-x|\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}})\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+1-2x+{x}^{2}}})\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x-1|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd5d1a-eeae-58f5-b7a1-a6a20fb02df9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8370" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =  5\\arsech{2x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsech x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5(-\\frac{1}{(2x)\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/id #uuid "83b6c061-a8fc-5628-a199-60196b904407" :question/math-academy-id "e-8371" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\arcoth{e^x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcoth x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "8a1806e8-d99d-5107-aa63-0bf841cb44c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8372" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $f(x) = \\sin{x} \\cdot \\arcsch{x},$ then $f'(x) = \\cos{x} \\arcsch{x} + g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$  is a product $u(x) \\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x) = \\sin{x}$ and $v(x) = \\arcsch{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x) = -\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520289} :answer-field/id #uuid "64aa8422-e168-5f7f-b4b2-8eebac1df31f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8788c2a-c953-5587-a4b0-071fdea7bf08" :question/math-academy-id "q-313233" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|x|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|2x|\\sqrt{1+(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|x|}\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0cd6cc1-2306-5ff5-bd40-675798a9d210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0cd6cc1-2306-5ff5-bd40-675798a9d210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520213} :answer-field/id #uuid "520cf314-e244-5017-a78d-80675136c535" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8198f6db-6c5f-5983-9cb0-0bd0190f9596" :question/math-academy-id "q-341473" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+4|\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{2}+4)}^{2}}}\\cdot {({x}^{2}+4)}^{′}-\\frac{{({x}^{2}+4)}^{′}}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+4)\\sqrt{1+({x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+16)}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+4)\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\cot x}{\\sqrt{1+\\sin^4 x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\cot x}{\\sqrt{1+\\sin^4 x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520342} :answer-field/id #uuid "404a0d84-133e-5c7d-befe-504815e54709" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84e76c93-4252-53d8-b14a-d598aa6e8e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-341483" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|{sin}^{2}⁡x|\\sqrt{1+{({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}}}]\\cdot {({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520130} :answer-field/id #uuid "c873029d-a874-5147-92bb-16fa73e1b639" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e713a272-c241-525b-b381-4fe5ba553286" :question/math-academy-id "q-341507" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520297} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf9bdaf-0642-5a54-b951-2e09ed88b490" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56abd260-e88d-5e15-85ad-d09d0617c5fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341509" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x})] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{2}}}]\\cdot {(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520043} :answer-field/id #uuid "465397d6-a020-5d18-96a2-fa78f2cfd4d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83895ad6-7f6a-50d5-a3b6-af8475bcabcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-341514" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}}]\\cdot {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡x}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c01ef25-72cb-56e3-850f-f5b42b06cd2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x(1+x)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520057} {:answer/id #uuid "578cf9cd-0a48-54e7-91c9-36e1da945aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520129} {:answer/id #uuid "5fffb130-9b68-531c-b156-aeb0418f3acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520141} {:answer/id #uuid "beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520257} {:answer/id #uuid "e95dd13d-e8b2-5d40-a5e7-9171f4068764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520257} :answer-field/id #uuid "35e861d8-35db-5fbf-9625-ffbf188c