⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
